# Full Stack Floor Map (Floors)

Extension for `@luizsantiago/fullstack-floor-map`. Requires Spec Seatbelt (`agent-architecture.md`).

## Layer registry (Floors)

Read `.specs/project/PROJECT.md` § **Layer registry** before each Execute task. One layer skill per turn: **frontend**, **backend**, **data**, **analytics**, **datascience**.

| Task `Files` vs registry | Load | Do not load |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Matches **one** layer | That `*-engineering.md` | Other layer skills |
| Matches **zero** layers | Neither — `engineering-standards.md` only | Layer skills |
| Matches **two or more** | **STOP** — split task | All layer skills |

Always keep Seatbelt `engineering-standards.md` + `references/implement.md`.

## Specialist catalog (optional depth)

After the layer manual, load **at most one** catalog `SKILL.md` suited to that Floor + § Stack / `Files`. Open **≤2** `references/` files.

Catalog `metadata.domain` → Floor (allow if mapped): `frontend`→frontend; `backend`|`api-architecture`→backend; `data-ml`→data|analytics|datascience; `language`→any Floor when Files/stack fit. Other domains (devops, security, quality, …) only if they clearly serve this Floor’s Execute work — **never** on `/verify`.

Specialists do not override task `Gate` or `PROJECT.md` test commands. Discover APIs from the repo.

## Pairing

Vertical **feature**, horizontal **tasks**. Run `npx @luizsantiago/fullstack-floor-map validate-layers <feature>` (= `python3 .specs/seatbelt/scripts/validate_layer_routing.py`).

## After commit / Verify

Drop layer + specialist. On **/verify**: no Floors, no catalog — Seatbelt Verify only.

## Re-install

Seatbelt does not delete Floors skills. Re-run `npx @luizsantiago/fullstack-floor-map install` to refresh.
